###
The Lennard-Jones equation of state at one state point, from the fits of
Thol et al.: pressure, energy, heat capacities, chemical potential and
activity for the full potential, the same moved to the potential cut (not
shifted) at 2.5 sigma by the long-range and delta corrections, and for the
potential cut and shifted at 2.5 sigma, with the residual free energy and
its derivatives behind each. These are the numbers Allen and Tildesley's
simulations are tested against.

This is eos_lj of Allen and Tildesley's examples for Computer Simulation
of Liquids (2nd ed., Oxford University Press, 2017;
https://github.com/Allen-Tildesley/examples), ported to Viv. The fits are
M. Thol, G. Rutkai, A. Koester, R. Lustig, R. Span and J. Vrabec, Journal
of Physical and Chemical Reference Data 45, 023101 (2016) (full potential)
and M. Thol, G. Rutkai, R. Span, J. Vrabec and R. Lustig, International
Journal of Thermophysics 36, 25 (2015) (cut and shifted); cite those for
the equation of state.
###
# The program behind `vp.liquids.eos` (eos_lj.export.toml).
#
#     viv run ports/liquids/eos_lj.viv
#
# Derived from eos_lj.f90 of https://github.com/Allen-Tildesley/examples
# (commit 4818bc82), by Michael P. Allen and Dominic J. Tildesley, CC0-1.0;
# see ports/liquids/LICENSE.
from ports.liquids.eos import a_res_full, a_res_cutshift, state_point, cut_from_full

#: temperature  the temperature, in units of epsilon / k_B
temperature = 1.0
#: density  the number density, in sigma^-3
density = 0.75

if temperature <= 0.0 or density <= 0.0 {
    stop(f"temperature and density must be positive; they are {temperature} and {density}")
}

a_f = a_res_full(temperature, density)
full = state_point(a_f, temperature, density)
cut = cut_from_full(full, temperature, density)
a_cs = a_res_cutshift(temperature, density)
cs = state_point(a_cs, temperature, density)

# ---- the full potential
#: p_full  the pressure
p_full = full.p
#: e_full  the energy per atom, with the ideal gas's 3T/2
e_full = full.e
#: cv_full  the heat capacity per atom at constant volume, in units of k_B
cv_full = full.cv
#: cp_full  the heat capacity per atom at constant pressure
cp_full = full.cp
#: mu_full  the chemical potential
mu_full = full.mu
#: z_full  the activity, exp(mu / T) in units of the thermal wavelength cubed
z_full = full.z
#: a_res_full_table  the table tau^i delta^j d^(i+j) a_res / d tau^i d delta^j, rows i and columns j from 0 to 2 (entries with i + j > 2 are not used)
a_res_full_table = a_f

# ---- cut (not shifted) at 2.5 sigma, from the full fit
#: p_cut  the pressure
p_cut = cut.p
#: e_cut  the energy per atom
e_cut = cut.e
#: mu_cut  the chemical potential
mu_cut = cut.mu
#: z_cut  the activity
z_cut = cut.z

# ---- cut and shifted at 2.5 sigma
#: p_cs  the pressure
p_cs = cs.p
#: e_cs  the energy per atom
e_cs = cs.e
#: cv_cs  the heat capacity per atom at constant volume
cv_cs = cs.cv
#: cp_cs  the heat capacity per atom at constant pressure
cp_cs = cs.cp
#: mu_cs  the chemical potential
mu_cs = cs.mu
#: z_cs  the activity
z_cs = cs.z
#: a_res_cs_table  the cut-and-shifted fit's table, as a_res_full
a_res_cs_table = a_cs

print(f"T = {temperature}  rho = {density}")
print(f"full:          P = {fmt(p_full, '.6f')}  E/N = {fmt(e_full, '.6f')}  Cv/N = {fmt(cv_full, '.6f')}  Cp/N = {fmt(cp_full, '.6f')}  mu = {fmt(mu_full, '.6f')}  z = {fmt(z_full, '.6f')}")
print(f"cut:           P = {fmt(p_cut, '.6f')}  E/N = {fmt(e_cut, '.6f')}  mu = {fmt(mu_cut, '.6f')}  z = {fmt(z_cut, '.6f')}")
print(f"cut-and-shift: P = {fmt(p_cs, '.6f')}  E/N = {fmt(e_cs, '.6f')}  Cv/N = {fmt(cv_cs, '.6f')}  Cp/N = {fmt(cp_cs, '.6f')}  mu = {fmt(mu_cs, '.6f')}  z = {fmt(z_cs, '.6f')}")

test "the heat capacities are positive and C_p exceeds C_v in the one-phase region" {
    assert_true(cv_full > 0.0 and cp_full > cv_full)
    assert_true(cv_cs > 0.0 and cp_cs > cv_cs)
}

